"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Amherst County shows August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of the 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 141% of normal in January to February and 43% in October to November. So far in 2026 it sits at 52% in March to April and 59% in April to May. Grid 20903 has a preliminary estimate of 48.0 for August to September 2026, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
